{
    "background_story": "Hunny was the proud name of the strongest and most resilient merlon in the ancient castle walls of Ashwood. A merlon is a solid portion of a battlement, and Hunny was the largest and most imposing of them all. For centuries, she stood watch over the kingdom, protecting its people from invaders and harsh weather. Her stone surface was weathered to a warm golden brown, and her crenels (notches) seemed to smile bravely in the face of adversity. Hunny had seen generations come and go, and her steadfast presence had become a symbol of the kingdom's enduring spirit. Despite the passing of time, Hunny remained unshakeable, a testament to the ingenuity and craftsmanship of the castle's long-forgotten builders.",
